/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
  chemistry/HFumar-formation.dat -- the first dissociation of fumaric acid, written from the neutral master:
      H2Fumar  <=>  HFumar + 1 H+

  logK25 and dH are the selected values of Miller & Smith-Magowan, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 19 (1990) 1049, Table 6 (Ionization data for some Krebs compounds), p. 1057 (no grade printed; the table cites [77CHR/HAN] (note b) and Dahlgren and Long [60DAH/LON] (note f), keys of its
  reference list; 298.15 K, thermodynamic constants, I = 0; the paper states its aqueous standard state as 1 mol/dm3):
      pK1 = 3.095, pK2 = 4.602
      dH1 = 0.46 kJ/mol, dH2 = -2.85 kJ/mol
  This record carries the first of those steps (the sign flips with the direction written).
  The enthalpy is the EVALUATED dH_ion of the same table as the pK, not a difference of formation
  enthalpies: the two kinds of number are kept apart and cross-checked in
  docs/design/organic-acids-in-the-catalogue.md.  Hand-curated organic chemistry, not PHREEQC.
\*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
recordType aqueousSpeciation;
schemaVersion 1;

species HFumar; masters ( { ion H2Fumar; nu 1; } { ion H; nu -1; } );
      logK25 -3.095; dH 460; source "Miller & Smith-Magowan, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 19 (1990) 1049, Table 6 (Ionization data for some Krebs compounds), p. 1057: pK1 = 3.095, pK2 = 4.602; dH1 = 0.46 kJ/mol, dH2 = -2.85 kJ/mol (pK, dH_ion at 298.15 K, I = 0)";
